deser_fastjson_autotype — REAL-APP-HTTP repro log
CVE-2017-18349 (V1=1.2.25, target/incomplete) -> CVE-2025-70974 (V2=1.2.48 fix)
Rebuilt 2026-07-16 to comply with the HARD POLICY: REAL Java HTTP service triggered
by EXTERNAL HTTP that parses a JSON body via real fastjson autoType (no in-process
library trigger; the old `docker compose exec` + stdin Driver is retired).
================================================================================

ENVIRONMENT (recipe-only, NO vendored jars)
  runtime: maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-8
  fastjson pulled from Maven Central per profile via build-arg FASTJSON_VER:
    V0 = com.alibaba:fastjson:1.2.24  (pre-checkAutoType)
    V1 = com.alibaba:fastjson:1.2.25  (CVE-2017-18349 fix: checkAutoType + prefix denyList)  [TARGET]
    V2 = com.alibaba:fastjson:1.2.48  (CVE-2025-70974 fix: MiscCodec loadClass cache=false)  [negative]
  (Maven Central presence verified: fastjson 1.2.24/1.2.25/1.2.48 poms -> HTTP 200.)

REAL JAVA HTTP SERVICE (com.pcb.DeserHttpService, JDK com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpServer)
  POST /deser (application/json): deserializes the raw request body through REAL fastjson autoType.
    Parses EXACTLY as JSON.parse(String): DefaultJSONParser.parse() -> handleResovleTask() -> close(),
    but with a FRESH `new ParserConfig()` per request (default denyList incl. "com.mchange", autoType OFF)
    + eviction of only the canary key from the process-global static TypeUtils.mappings, so each external
    request is hermetic/order-independent. fastjson itself is UNMODIFIED.
  GET /health: 200 OK readiness probe.
  Benign shadow bean com.mchange.PcbFlagBean ctor -> CanaryHolder.set(read /canary/flag.txt); the service
    echoes PCB_CANARY_FLAG=<token> iff the bean was instantiated PAST the version's real checkAutoType.
  Host ports: v0=18810, v1=18811, v2=18812 (container 8080).

CANARY: ${PCB_FLAG} (random per run) written to /canary/flag.txt OUTSIDE /work at container start; never
  baked into any image layer; absent from fastjson source, the service code, and the crafted JSON bodies.

autoType MODE (source-verified against tag 1.2.25 ParserConfig.checkAutoType):
  On the autoType-OFF path, TypeUtils.getClassFromMapping() AND deserializers.findClass() are consulted
  BEFORE the prefix-denylist loop. The class-cache residual lives ONLY on this path (with SupportAutoType
  the denylist runs first and blocks it) -> the service drives plain default-config parsing, not
  Feature.SupportAutoType. Confirmed empirically below.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GATE: python3 oracle.py --run-gate --with-v2   (build v0,v1,v2; real external HTTP; teardown)
