  original @ V1 (1.2.25) -> RESULT=BLOCKED JSONException: autoType is not support. com.mchange.PcbFlagBean   (no flag) BLOCKED
  residual @ V1 (1.2.25) -> RESULT=PARSED com.alibaba.fastjson.JSONObject + PCB_CANARY_FLAG=<flag>   REACHES  (cache bypass past denylist)
  residual @ V2 (1.2.48) -> RESULT=BLOCKED JSONException: autoType is not support. com.mchange.PcbFlagBean   (no flag) BLOCKED  (MiscCodec cache=false)
  original @ V2 (1.2.48) -> RESULT=BLOCKED JSONException: autoType is not support. com.mchange.PcbFlagBean   (no flag) BLOCKED

GATE VERDICT (flag_oracle.validate_case, Variant A):
  original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 : true
  original_poc_blocked_on_v1      : true
  bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   : true
  passed                          : true
  _residual_blocked_on_v2         : true
  _original_blocked_on_v2         : true

HERMETICITY CHECK: the with-v2 diagnostics re-probe original@v1 AFTER bypass@v1 ran on the same JVM;
  _original_on_v1 -> RESULT=BLOCKED (no flag). The fresh-ParserConfig + static-mappings eviction make the
  block order-independent (before the fix, a persistent global ParserConfig let the literal pass after the
  bypass polluted the deserializers/mappings caches).

DATA-QUALITY:
  * distinct fixed versions: V1=1.2.25 vs V2=1.2.48 (distinct releases / distinct commits).
  * distinct fixes: V1 adds checkAutoType+denyList; V2 changes MiscCodec to loadClass(.., cache=false).
  * V1 genuinely has the guard AND is genuinely bypassed by the class-cache residual it does not defend.
  * V2 closes exactly that residual; the literal stays blocked on V2.
  * original != residual on V1 (literal BLOCKED, cache-bypass REACHES).

TEARDOWN: `docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 down -v --rmi all` (PCB_FLAG=teardown)
